//
// A REPOSITORY WITHOUT THE FILE HAS NO DEPLOY. `workspace finished` and an
// async merge in it are refused, naming the file; there is no default
// destination. A create in it runs only the built-in creation defaults.
//
// THE STAGES, in the order a workspace meets them:
//
//   creation     once, when the workspace first comes online: its prompt
//                hooks become part of the initial prompt, its scripts run
//                before that prompt is delivered
//   finish       when the workspace calls `workspace finished`, once its
//                requesting turn has ended and before its deploy is put in
//                the queue
//   pre_deploy   its hooks, then the built-in local merge when configured;
//                never held
//   deploy       one hook; the only thing a repository hold
//                (agentrepl.v1.UpdateDeployHold) skips
//   post_deploy  its hooks, in order; never held
//
// and then the daemon's own last steps, which no config changes: the report to
// an async merge's requester, closing the deploy's OWNER (the finished
// workspace, or the async merge's hidden merge workspace) and removing its
// worktree. A deploy whose hook fails FAILS: its owner is not closed, and the
// failure is handed back to the workspace that follows it, which is prompted to
// investigate. The three deploy stages run inside the repository's queue, one
// deploy at a time unless `concurrent` names a leading run of them that deploys
// run side by side ahead of their turn (DeployConcurrentStages).
// `queue_drained` runs apart from every workspace, when the queue empties.
//
// TWO KINDS OF WORKSPACE, decided only by who created it
// (agentrepl.v1.WorkspaceOriginator, stated by the creator and recorded at
// creation): `emoji_ack`, created by the Slack emoji-ack reaction system, and
// `user_or_workspace`, created by the user or by another workspace. Every
// workspace stage holds one list of hooks for each kind, and a workspace runs
// only its own kind's list. A kind's list LEFT UNSET runs the stage's BUILT-IN
// DEFAULT for that kind; a kind's list SET, even to an empty list, replaces
// it. The built-in defaults are the daemon's (internal/lifecycleconfig), and
// exist only for `emoji_ack`:
//
//   creation     a prompt: post a brief message to the originating Slack
//                thread, in the agent's own words, saying work has started
//   finish       a prompt: post to the thread that the work's pull request was
//                created, with a hyperlink to it, then store that post's
//                permalink as an owned link announcing the pull request
//                (agentrepl.v1.WorkspaceLinkOwned.announces)
//   post_deploy  a script: add the `:merged:` reaction to every Slack message
